WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
They didn’t have any colors for the game . . . for the team.

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:13.060
So there was a boy that selected blue and white but that didn’t approve . . . appeal to anybody and nobody had even really thought about it.

3
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:29.980
So, my father [Charles E. Coates] shopped around at various stores on Third Street and they had some ribbon left over from the Mardi Gras celebration.

4
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:30.738
But all they had were purple and gold, the green was gone.

5
00:00:30.738 --> 00:00:34.940
So he selected the purple and gold which we still use.

6
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.280
And then somebody said to him, “Well, what about a name?”

7
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:50.400
And there was a contingent of Louisiana men who made a very valiant and valuable contribution to the [Civil] War.

8
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.140
They called them the Louisiana Tigers.

9
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.780
And so my father said, “Well, we’ll call our team The Tigers.”
